Join records without inventing or losing observations (@rc-joins: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @reproducible-computation, #source "../sources/Good-Research-Code.lingua#r_771ZMSHAY1TCSTFCHPT9KZRA66", #source "../sources/Scientific-Computing-Practices.lingua#r_5J8HXCQDNJH59EZC1PRJTQK38B", #reproducible-computation "Identity-hashes-and-originals.lingua#r_39P9KR6GAJ6ST89N2JXND7HBCX") { r_49F957J1ZP9JVG5KQSET12P4PH
**Read:** [The Good Research Code Handbook — Mineault and community](../sources/Good-Research-Code.lingua#r_771ZMSHAY1TCSTFCHPT9KZRA66), project organization and decoupled transformations; [Good enough practices in scientific computing — Wilson and colleagues](../sources/Scientific-Computing-Practices.lingua#r_5J8HXCQDNJH59EZC1PRJTQK38B), data organization, programming, and collaboration sections.

A join combines records according to a key and a declared relationship. A one-to-one lot table and assay table require unique keys on both sides. A one-to-many relationship may be valid for repeated specimens, but summing the duplicated lot mass afterwards would invent material. Inspect cardinality rather than accepting a library's default join as the scientific method.

Count rows and distinct identities before and after a join. Examine unmatched keys, duplicate keys, and columns with the same name but different meanings. A lot sampled twice needs an explicit model for combining assays or treating specimens separately. The row count alone does not establish representativeness or correct weighting.

Units, time, and basis can function like hidden keys. Matching a pressure value with a temperature measured an hour later may violate a supposedly simultaneous correction. A local timestamp needs its offset or time-zone interpretation for cross-site work. A mass reported in tonnes must be converted deliberately before combination with kilograms. A dry-basis assay should not be merged with wet mass without its conversion information.

**Work:** split the teaching CSV into a lot table and an assay table. Introduce a duplicate assay and an unmatched lot. State expected counts and rejection rules before joining them, then show how a careless join would change the total component mass. Reconstruct one corrected join manually. Add timestamps and specify the time relation necessary for a defensible association.

For a large scientific table, encode these expectations in checks that fail with interpretable diagnostics. Preserve the mapping of original identities even if a publication uses anonymized keys. The scientific question determines the association; a convenient common text column does not.

**Continue:** [Preserve originals and distinguish identity from location](Identity-hashes-and-originals.lingua#r_39P9KR6GAJ6ST89N2JXND7HBCX).

